  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered"><span class="username">Chamilka</span>, You Are The <span class="archetype">Ruler</span> - <span class="text-orange">And This Is What It Means...</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/it-means.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>The Ruler archetype is best defined by its innate ability to lead. While others tend to avoid playing the role of a leader, Rulers are absolutely comfortable with volunteering to take charge.</p>
              <p>It's important to note that it's not the desire to lead that defines the Ruler archetype, but the actual quality of leadership that you are able to administer.</p>
              <p>Truth be told, the Ruler archetype is not merely one-dimensional. It has <span class="text-orange">many different sides and faces</span>, and as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction, you'll begin to understand what I mean. But before we proceed, please do so with with an open mind, and a willing heart.</p>
              <p><span class="username"></span>, the Ruler archetype is best illustrated through the decisions that you make. You are often fair, just, and honourable.</p>
              <p>You're able to manage the expectations of others and grant direction towards maintaining order amongst your friends and various groups of people.</p>
              <p>But what really sets you apart is your passion for power and authority... <span class="text-orange">Control is the one thing that you sought after the most</span>, and also the one thing that you find the most fulfilling.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Everything that you do is always somehow related to either gaining, maintaining, or even exercising control. That does not mean to say that you're a control freak. Your approach to idea of control is calculated and methodical.</p>
          <p>More often than not, you leverage on your leadership qualities to attain higher personal goals, be it for their family, friends, or your community, and not for senseless or selfish reasons.</p>
          <p>If there's anyone who's capable of pulling that off, it's you, and you know that as well.</p>
          <p>Others find themselves drawn to you because of your assertive and decisive personality. Within your group of friends, you are often the one calling the shots and organizing outings and gatherings... A trait that others find alluring and attractive about you.</p>
          <p>Needless to say, the Ruler is perhaps one of the most charismatic archetypes. After all, you do need a little bit of charisma in order to gain the trust of others.</p>
          <p><span class="username"></span>, you are also idealistic when it comes to your goals - a strong sign of a visionary.</p>
          <p>You refuse to fall short of your objectives, and you consider consolation as an indicator of failure.</p>
          <p>As a Ruler, you thrive on creating reliable systems for others to follow.</p>
          <p>Your stance is grounded with conviction, and that conviction is articulated with <span class="text-orange">empathy, kindness, and a giving heart</span>.</p>
          <p>Your visions are what drive you and motivate you to live life to its fullest. And you refuse to rest until you see your visions through.</p>
          <p>You feel responsible for the others around you - whether they're your friends, co-workers, or even your loved ones. That sense of responsibility pushes you to lead them by example. And that's what ultimately separates you from the wannabes.</p>
          <p>But we'll discuss that in greater detail as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Ruler</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>The Ruler is a person of the people, owed in part to your extroverted mindset. You have an uncanny ability to learn the emotions of other people, and then use it for your own advantage. Unsurprisingly, <span class="text-orange">you can come across as manipulative</span>, but if you are able to play to this particular strength correctly and benevolently, you will be amply rewarded with friends and emotional connections.</p>
              <p>Predictably, you possess an ego of sorts. You are proud of yourself and often prioritize your needs over other people. The rationale behind this is somewhat universal: the safety of the Ruler is paramount in order to lead, but nevertheless, this can give way to potential conflicts as people might wrongly think you care only about your own gain.</p>
              <p>The Ruler wants nothing more than a rational world guided by a <span class="text-orange">strong sense of order</span>, and this is exactly why you tend to embody this philosophy into everything that you do. Rather than act on impulse, you act with cold calculation and treat everything around you as information that could either be detrimental or useful to you in some way. This makes you logical, but also appear somewhat cold.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Though you possess a cold exterior, you can be surprisingly understanding and empathetic of others deep down. It may take a while for people to unlock this side of you, but the fact that it’s there also means that you are subject to all the anxieties associated with turbulence such as self-doubt. Often, you will question yourself and everything you stand for, and you will need your friends to overcome them.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1,2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Ruler, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As an extroverted personality, the Ruler archetype is known for having assertiveness as one of its greatest strengths. What this means is that you are the sort of person who will gladly argue your points with others.</p>
              <p>When in an argument, you won’t find yourself back down. As a matter of fact, the more you are questioned, the more you push yourself into finding a meaningful answer to make sure that whatever your decision is at that moment will be infallible and perfectly accurate.</p>
              <p>This natural desire to assert oneself in any social context will do you a lot of favors to people, as they are often drawn to those who can <span class="text-orange">defend themselves in a heated discussion</span>. The fact that you believe in yourself and your ideas enough to actually defend them tooth and nail will certainly help you make a lot of like-minded friends.</p>
              <p>As egocentric types, Rulers often understand their feelings above anything else. They are also extremely aware when they’re being emotional or being logical. This unique ability to separate facts from feelings is what gives them clarity.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>In a way, this clarity helps you a lot especially during <span class="text-orange">tense situations</span> where you are forced to do something rapidly. People in tense situations can be more emotional than logical, and as a Ruler, you are ready to put your foot down and tell everyone that they’re using their emotions more than their minds.</p>
          <p>Naturally, this clear thought pattern allows you to become a beacon of logic for all the others who might need it. When in a team, you will be unafraid to criticize or call out illogical statements, and thus, you’re often seen as an important component of any team’s victory.</p>
          <p>Rationality demands that one be persuasive in their arguments with other people. Having the gall to defend your stand is just part of the equation; you also need to make sure you have enough facts to persuade.</p>
          <p>Luckily, you have dominion over this area. As a Ruler, you are acutely aware that having authority means being factual. As such, you will be well-read in any topic you engage in. In fact, even in general knowledge, you’ll also have a likely edge since you understand that you also need to be well-rounded to rule properly.</p>
          <p>You also possess a <span class="text-orange">natural talent for explaining things in an understandable fashion</span>, more than just logic and knowledge. As an element of persuasion, you understand that you need to be clear in your language. You hate verbosity, and you want to go straight to the point. This makes you effective at bringing people to your side.</p>
          <p>Having a turbulent personality means that you need some sort of anchor to make sure that wherever the winds of your personality take you, you will always have a constant to focus on. As it turns out, this is another department in which the Ruler excels.</p>
          <p>In connection to your deep need for control, you often structure your life in such a way that you have goals to accomplish every single day. For example, you often map out how many hours of sleep you’re going to get in a day or how many chapters you’re going to read before ending it.</p>
          <p>More importantly, however, is the fact that when you’re put in a team, you are likely going to try and map out goals for your team as well. In some ways, people might think you’re bossy for this, but it’s this exact penchant for goal-setting that naturally allows a team to truly thrive. Whatever criticism you might get initially for doing this will quickly be overturned by support from other people later.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Ruler, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your turbulent nature, you are often emotional. Whereas other archetypes tend to be logical and reasonable, you are inclined to be more creative and emotionally-dictated. </p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, this tendency will bring flavor. As such, you may often seek to have intimate, emotionally charged moments with your partner. Everything that goes in your relationship is going to matter because your emotions will compel you to care about the smallest details.</p>
              <p>Given this, you are likely to look for someone who can <span class="text-orange">empathize with this feeling</span>. The questions that will govern you as you seek a life partner is whether they have enough empathy to put themselves on your shoes.</p>
              <p>This also affects the way you end up solving problems together. As the Ruler, you may have a public persona that’s strong and bold, but in private conversation, you may be significantly more affectionate and fragile with your emotions. This is because you feel a sense of security when you are with someone you truly like.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That besides, however, there is a <span class="text-orange">problem with this emotional link</span>. Although it is healthy to be honest with your feelings towards someone, the downside becomes when you are too governed by your emotion to solve problems rationally.</p>
          <p>This means that you may end up regularly arguing with your significant other about certain things, such as cheating. You might become easily suspicious if you see your partner hanging out with other people.</p>
          <p>This sort of feeling stems from a need for control, and although this is perfectly understandable, the problem starts when you become too possessive of the person you are with. To be clear, being emotional isn’t a bad thing at all-- it’s necessary because love is truly about emotions, but you should never forget to hold onto your rational side when the situation calls for it. This way, your relationship will thrive.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Looking at the core qualities of your archetype, we’ll see a Ruler who desires the absolute best in any given situation. To them, <span class="text-orange">being in a superior spot always means being in control</span>, and this will manifest undoubtedly as being demanding in a relationship.</p>
          <p>This trait often manifests in your likelihood to regularly test your partner’s abilities and loyalty. You can be demanding in terms of what to look for in a date, and you can be especially demanding once the relationship takes off.</p>
          <p>All of this stems from the need to simply see things being stable. Although the primary purpose of this trait stems from control, it’s really only the case because control gives stability. In other words, you are consciously setting up high expectations because you do not want you relationship to simply flounder.</p>
          <p>Viewed in this light, your demanding attitude can be a positive thing. It means that you will regularly grow with your partner and that you won’t allow your relationship to run stale under any circumstances. You will always find something to do and be happy about, and you will always expect great things from your great equal.</p>
          <p>However, this attitude can also <span class="text-orange">open the doors to oppression and tyranny</span> in a relationship. If you aren’t careful, your partner may come to fear and even hate your domination of them.</p>
          <p>As such, when you do need to be demanding, you should demand for the right things. Be reasonable when failures occur, as while you can be in a perfect relationship with someone, the reality is that no one person is ever perfect on their own. Your partner is going to make some mistakes too, so you should lower the bar as necessary to keep the relationship going.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Ruler is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Ruler</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Ruler is a combination of extroversion, egocentrism, rationality, and turbulence. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to managerial work, politics, and entrepreneurship. With their authoritative nature, Rulers will undoubtedly excel at these jobs. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them. </p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/project-manager-ruler.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Project Manager</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Rulers are best suited as managers. Because they have the natural knack to guide others through any storm, they’ll find it natural to be in a powerful position to do so.</p>
              <p>In any discipline, there is a need to instill order and stability to make sure that everything works perfectly well. At the bare minimum, a leader should be able to persuade their comrades to do what they want them to do and command their total respect and loyalty.</p>
              <p>This is a particularly important fact when it comes to projects, as it can be amazingly difficult to bring a diverse group of people together for tasks that require some time to work on. Working as a group can be a particularly stressful experience, and as project manager, the one thing you should be capable of doing is bringing your diverse group of individuals together and whip them into shape as a unit.</p>
              <p>Further, being in this setup emphasizes the fact that you can’t just win on your own. You need to be able to rely on your whole team, and while you do have this capacity, this can be swiftly swept aside by office politics and drama, of which you will also be likely at the center. In other words, being project manager will truly put to the test your ability to mitigate the effects of workplace drama on your teammates’ focus-- something that you are already well-equipped for.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>The last thing that a project manager will surely bring out in you is the ability to delegate tasks. In your case, since you are an extroverted character, you will be able to read people and actually be socially adept enough to know who is more useful for certain tasks. Each person has their own strengths and weaknesses which can influence how efficient your team will be-- and will be your goal to manage them.</p>
          <p>In other words, being a project manager will do wonders for you because it will put you in a position where you can truly stand out in a limited environment. You will be working with just enough people to actually know intimately enough, while also being able to think of the larger picture, far beyond the team’s aims. Use your time and power wisely in this role, and your career will truly be perfect.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/politic-ruler.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Politician</h5>
              <p>In ancient times, the most common form of government tended to be the monarchy. This governmental system believed that rulers were divinely mandated by God (or Heaven) to rule upon their constituents. Their word was law, and ordinary subjects had to obey from afar, to the point where their own welfare depended upon the benevolence of their ruler.</p>
              <p>This system was eventually overturned in most countries, until the dominant form of government became democracy. With this evolution came the fact that politicians now depended upon their people-- not their infallibility-- for support. In other words, politicians are meant to lead their people-- for their own welfare-- a role that you as a Ruler will truly thrive and even improve as a person in.</p>
              <p>This means that you will need to control your self-centeredness in order to think about the common good. The more you commit yourself to justice and the rule of law, the better your standing will be among the people, and the more you’ll be able to truly live up to your ruling nature.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Aside from this, it will also be the ultimate test of your charisma. Rulers and politicians alike need to be able to appeal to their voters both in a creative and political sense. As such, you can’t just be a good worker-- you have to step up and truly become a political leader.</p>
          <p>When you do find yourself pursuing politics, always remember that you are beholden to the people-- and as long as you truly work for them, not only will you be able to improve their lives, you’ll be able to fulfill your secondary aim of having a legacy worth emulating.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/entrepreneur-ruler.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Entrepreneur</h5>
              <p>It may seem a bit weird that Rulers would make for good entrepreneurs, but this is actually closer to the Ruler’s true nature than one might expect. This is because entrepreneurship requires a harmonious combination of leadership, charisma, tact and especially the final ingredient: innovation.</p>
              <p>As you may have guessed, being of this particular archetype means being innovative and dynamic, as no leader can ever stand perfectly still and rigid for all time. They have to be adaptable to changes, negative or positive, and since they have a mandate as leaders, they also need to be the trend-setters that will naturally revolutionize or even start an entirely new movement in any field you’re passionate about.</p>
              <p>Likewise, since you’re starting from a clean slate, it will also be a great opportunity for you to expand your general knowledge and enhance your authority. If you didn’t already have an idea of economics, you’ll have to go and study some of the basics in order to inform yourself and have an excellent idea as to where you will start. Since you are a rational person, you’ll be able to piece together something that will truly work.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Further, since you are extroverted, it will be easy for you to actually expand your social networks as well as your general know-how. Having good people around you will effectively ensure that you will have plenty of ideas to work with. Together with your own personal genius, there is nothing that you can’t accomplish. The only thing that you will have to overcome is your own self-centeredness.</p>
          <p>Granted, it won’t be easy. Self-centeredness is foremost in a Ruler’s nature and doesn’t work in an age of globalization and cooperation. But if you are able to overcome this weakness, you will indeed be able to bring something new to the table.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span> and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-4" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(4,5)">Show Me Now</a>
